{"page":"GSDMB","gene":"GSDMB","accession":"Q8TAX9","protein":"Gasdermin-B","length":416,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q8TAX9-4","name":"4","synonyms":["GSDMB3","Isoform 4"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Precursor of a pore-forming protein that acts as a downstream mediator of granzyme-mediated cell death and mediates pyroptosis (PubMed:28154144, PubMed:36157507, PubMed:36899106, PubMed:36991122, PubMed:36991125). Following cleavage and activation by granzyme A (GZMA), the N-terminal part binds to membrane inner leaflet lipids, homooligomerizes within the human plasma membrane and forms pores of 10-15 nanometers (nm) of inner diameter, triggering pyroptosis (PubMed:28154144, PubMed:36157507, PubMed:36899106, PubMed:36991122, PubMed:36991125). Recognizes and binds membrane inner leaflet lipids of human cells, such as phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate, phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate, bisphosphorylated phosphatidylinositols, such as phosphatidylinositol (4,5)-bisphosphate, and more weakly to phosphatidic acid (PubMed:28154144, PubMed:36157507). Also binds sufatide, a component of the apical membrane of epithelial cells (PubMed:28154144)"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000418519.6","ENST00000360317.7"],"refseq":["NM_001165958.2","NM_001388420.1"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001159430.1","NP_001375349.1"],"maneSelect":true},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8TAX9-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8TAX9-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":71.5,"plddt":[[50,2],[70,20],[90,1],[70,1],[90,1],[70,5],[90,1],[70,1],[90,3],[70,2],[90,4],[70,14],[90,2],[70,3],[90,1],[70,3],[50,5],[0,11],[50,1],[0,34],[50,4],[70,17],[90,3],[70,15],[90,6],[70,9],[50,5],[0,17],[50,4],[70,7],[90,2],[70,1],[90,9],[70,4],[90,3],[70,3],[50,3],[70,6],[50,1],[0,15],[50,3],[70,8],[90,6],[70,1],[90,3],[70,1],[90,12],[70,9],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,10],[50,1],[70,6],[90,7],[70,3],[90,7],[70,1],[90,6],[70,1],[90,2],[70,29],[50,5],[0,12],[50,4],[70,7],[90,9],[70,2],[50,1],[0,6]]}},"features":[{"type":"Chain","start":1,"end":244,"description":"Gasdermin-B, N-terminal"},{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":280,"description":"Triggers pyroptosis"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":83,"end":101,"description":"Beta stranded"},{"type":"Site","start":91,"end":92,"description":"Cleavage; by CAPS3, CAPS6 and CAPS9"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":102,"end":125,"description":"Beta stranded"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":166,"end":166,"description":"(Microbial infection) Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":167,"end":183,"description":"Beta stranded"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":177,"end":177,"description":"(Microbial infection) Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":184,"end":198,"description":"Beta stranded"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":190,"end":190,"description":"(Microbial infection) Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":192,"end":192,"description":"(Microbial infection) Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Site","start":220,"end":221,"description":"Cleavage; by ELANE"},{"type":"Site","start":229,"end":230,"description":"Cleavage; by granzyme A"},{"type":"Site","start":244,"end":245,"description":"Cleavage; by granzyme A"},{"type":"Chain","start":245,"end":416,"description":"Gasdermin-B, C-terminal"},{"type":"Coiled coil","start":248,"end":276,"description":""},{"type":"Cross-link","start":308,"end":308,"description":"(Microbial infection) Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"}],"interfaces":{},"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q8TAX9-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Precursor of a pore-forming protein that acts as a downstream mediator of granzyme-mediated cell death and specifically mediates cell death of Gram-negative bacteria in response to infection (PubMed:34022140). Following cleavage and activation by granzyme A (GZMA), the N-terminal part recognizes and binds phospholipids found on Gram-negative bacterial membranes, such as lipid A and cariolipin, homooligomerizes within the bacterial membranes and forms pores, triggering pyroptosis followed by cell death (PubMed:34022140). In contrast to isoform 4, does not bind to membrane inner leaflet lipids of host human cell, such as phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate, phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate, bisphosphorylated phosphatidylinositols, such as phosphatidylinositol (4,5)-bisphosphate (PubMed:34022140)"},{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"Non canonical splice junctions"}],"length":411,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false},"segments":[[1,1,220],[226,222,12],[238,243,174]],"edits":[{"start":221,"end":221,"original":"N","replacement":"SAGLD","added":5},{"start":234,"end":242,"original":"EKDGASSCL","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":9,"replaced":1,"novel":5,"foldedAbsent":1,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[0,9,1],[1,9,1],[11,0,1]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8TAX9-1-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8TAX9-1-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":71.1,"plddt":[[50,2],[70,16],[50,1],[70,5],[90,1],[70,5],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,2],[90,3],[70,23],[50,15],[0,4],[50,1],[0,32],[50,3],[70,16],[50,1],[70,14],[50,1],[70,1],[50,1],[70,4],[90,2],[70,11],[50,5],[0,15],[50,6],[70,8],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,6],[50,3],[0,2],[50,1],[0,3],[50,11],[70,1],[50,3],[0,5],[50,4],[70,8],[90,6],[70,1],[90,2],[70,2],[90,12],[70,9],[90,1],[70,3],[90,1],[70,10],[50,2],[70,5],[90,2],[70,1],[90,4],[70,3],[90,14],[70,2],[90,1],[70,4],[50,1],[70,22],[50,10],[0,7],[50,6],[70,7],[90,9],[70,2],[50,1],[0,6]],"losingConfidence":2}},{"accession":"Q8TAX9-2","name":"2","synonyms":["GSDMB2"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Not able to trigger pyroptosis"}],"length":394,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000394175.6","ENST00000901437.1"],"